# MicStage production release (Hostinger)

Production app: **https://micstage.com** (existing Hostinger Node.js site `u703718100` / `micstage.com`).
Do **not** create a new Hostinger site/app.

## Permanent release flow

1. Make the change
2. Test
3. Typecheck
4. Production build (`npm run build` — bakes `deployCommit` via `scripts/write-deploy-commit.mjs`)
5. Commit
6. Push `main`
7. **Hostinger deploy** the existing micstage.com app (`u703718100`) via Cursor Hostinger MCP `hosting_deployJsApplication` (or confirm/wait on the Git-triggered Hostinger build). **Do not stop after pushing to GitHub.**
8. Wait for Hostinger deployment to complete (`hosting_listJsDeployments` / wait scripts)
9. Verify `https://micstage.com/api/health` (`ok: true`, `deployCommit` = exact pushed short SHA)
10. Live smoke-test affected functionality
11. Report the deployed SHA

Do **not** start an archive deploy while another Hostinger build for micstage.com is already running.
Optional ops: `hosting_restartNode_jsApplicationV1` (restart only; does not rebuild).

## Do not auto-deploy when

- Tests fail
- Typecheck or production build fails
- A migration is destructive or data-risky (stop and get explicit approval)

## deployCommit

`/api/health` reports the Git short SHA baked at build time (`src/generated/deployCommit.ts`).
Do **not** manually update `DEPLOY_GIT_SHA` each release. Prefer removing that Hostinger env var in hPanel when convenient; never use the replace-all env API without the full secret set. Bake must not read `DEPLOY_GIT_SHA` (stale).

## Eligio rule

Eligio’s production Host data is **READ-ONLY** for debugging unless the user explicitly authorizes writes.
